<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The launcher background, and the one place a raw hex value is legitimate:
      an app icon is a fixed asset, not themed surface. Nothing in the app's own
      chrome may reference this.

      Off-white rather than a coloured tile. The mark drawn on top is the
      server's own logo, and it needs a neutral behind it: on the accent blue
      this icon started life on, the deepest violet of the default colourway
      very nearly disappeared. This is the light theme's surface value, so the
      icon and the app it opens are the same paper.

      One background for all thirty-two colourways, and it is a fixed off-white
      in every theme the phone can be in. That is what decides which half of
      LogoStyle the generated icons are painted from: the server publishes a
      light set of strokes and a dark set, and the dark set exists for a dark
      *page*. There is no dark page here — a launcher does not redraw an
      installed app's icon for dark mode — so the icons use the light strokes
      throughout, and the dark ones are not in the APK at all.

      The web's own PNG icons are the same mark on transparency, so there is no
      tile to copy from — `LogoStyle::tile()` exists for the theme-color meta
      rather than for the icons. Off-white is this app's answer to a question
      the web does not have to ask, an adaptive icon always having a background
      layer.
    -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#FAF9F7</color>
</resources>
